  "body": "`crates/app/tests/ai_guide.rs` `ai_guide_calls_match_live_tools_list` fails on Windows:\n\n```\npanicked at crates\\app\\tests\\ai_guide.rs:40:5:\nthe four tasks need complete tools/call examples\n```\n\nCause: the test splits `site/content/guide/automate/ai.md` on \"```json\\n\". A Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf` has CRLF line endings in that file (`file` reports \"with CRLF line terminators\"). Then no fence matches, and the call count is 0.\n\nFound in the quick gate of PR #3118 (Windows x86_64, upstream main 11402dba4). That PR does not touch the guide or the test.\n\nPossible fix: normalize the line endings after the read (`text.replace(\"\\r\\n\", \"\\n\")`), or add a `.gitattributes` rule for the guide files.\n\nProposed labels (a contributor cannot set labels): `bug`, `P5`, `effort:low`, `area:mcp`, `source:agent`. It blocks the quick gate of Windows contributors.\n\nDone means: the test passes on a Windows CRLF checkout and on Linux.\n",
